# ENGLISH: Template for the frontend's local environment file. What it
# does: documents every VITE_* variable the app reads (Vite only
# exposes env vars prefixed VITE_ to client code, by design - anything
# else stays server/build-only). Why it exists: "never commit secrets"
# - copy this to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in real
# values per developer machine; this file itself stays committed with
# placeholders only. How it will communicate with the backend:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is exactly what src/api/axiosClient.ts reads as its
# baseURL - the one setting that wires the frontend to this specific
# backend instance.
#
# HINGLISH: Frontend ki local environment file ka template. Ye kya
# karti hai: har VITE_* variable document karti hai jo app padhta hai
# (Vite sirf VITE_ prefix wale env vars ko client code me expose karta
# hai, design se - baaki sab server/build-only rehta hai). Ye dashboard
# me kyu hai: "never commit secrets" - ise .env.local me copy karo
# (pehle se gitignored hai) aur har developer machine ke liye real
# values bharo; ye file khud placeholders ke saath hi committed rehti
# hai. Backend se kaise connect hogi: VITE_API_BASE_URL exactly wahi
# hai jise src/api/axiosClient.ts apne baseURL ke roop me padhta hai -
# wahi ek setting jo frontend ko is specific backend instance se
# wire karti hai.

# Control Center backend base URL (see backend/src/main/resources/application.yml server.port)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8089

# Request timeout in milliseconds for API calls made via src/api/axiosClient.ts
VITE_API_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# Build/deploy environment label shown in the UI's environment indicator (dev/staging/prod)
VITE_APP_ENVIRONMENT=dev
